 past time. Regular forms often end in -ed; irregular forms must be learned.","examples":["We booked a room last week.","The visitor spoke to the guide."]},{"title":"Questions and negatives","explanation":"Did and did not carry the past tense. The main verb is the base form, even when its affirmative past is irregular.","examples":["Did the shop open early?","They did not bring a camera."]},{"title":"Spelling and unchanged forms","explanation":"Some verbs change spelling; others keep the same written form. Read has the same spelling in the present and past but different pronunciation.","examples":["carry → carried","put → put"]}],"tips":["Read the full context before choosing.","Check the explanation, including after a correct answer.","A passing practice session is useful feedback, not a language certificate."],"source":"seed","provenance":{"version":"foundations-2026-09-v1","authorship":"Grammacho; generated offline with AI assistance","kind":"original-guidance-aligned","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending","referenceIds":["bc-past","pcc-esol"],"assessment":"Practice only; levels are approximate teaching labels, not validated CEFR assessment."}}'::jsonb j) payload
